From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 14:32:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/29] function-runner: reserve dependency-only overflow
 capacity

Treat MAX_ISOLATE_WORKERS minus ISOLATE_DEPENDENCY_WORKER_RESERVE as shared
worker occupancy consumed by every request class. Admit only
ancestor-unblocking dependencies above that base, enforce the same bounded
rule per client, and keep the independent action-shell cap separate.

Preserve upstream's distinct direct nested-UDF path: it bypasses external
CoDel, is polled before external work, and acquires a high-priority active-
JavaScript permit before worker assignment. Keep bounded Q + R CoDel admission
for externally propagated dependencies, especially Node and action callback
chains. Both paths use the same physical worker total and dependency reserve;
neither adds active-JavaScript permits or a second worker pool.

Keep the standard tree's in-process runner as the capacity owner. Remove the
post-rebase runner capability flag and best-effort application action cap;
custom runners must provide equivalent bounded dependency admission at their
own pool instead of borrowing local isolate-worker knobs.

Propagate dependency ancestry through application, function-runner, V8, Node,
and trusted callback boundaries. Apply cancellation-safe shared-base admission
to application and HTTP limits, prevent query-cache coalescing from recreating
the inversion, and retain completion-first scheduler accounting and finite
external queue expiry.

Expose bounded scheduler capacity, class, overflow, expiry, rejection, source
occupancy, and effective per-executor parallelism metrics. Initialize closed
failure label sets at zero, reject invalid completion ownership and scheduled
parallelism, and document the composed upstream and self-hosted contract.
